      "sourceTextSha256": "afe33654583015f0c00b82953ed0ef688c95417f505bf8f76ffb4afeba03b50b",
      "text": "Day 7 · Jodensavanne, the “Jewish Savannah” on the Suriname River, was founded in the 17th century by Jewish planters who had fled the Inquisition in Spain and Portugal. Explore the ruins of the Beracha VeShalom synagogue, built in 1685 and one of the oldest in the Americas, and its weathered cemetery. Then visit Redi Doti, a small Arawak village whose people preserve their music, dance and traditional medicine, and, time permitting, their pineapple fields. Lunch included; back to your hotel. (B, L)",
